            "review_text": "mattthebeard1989\nWare, United Kingdom219 contributions\n0\nNice view, beer prices okay considering\nApr 2016 • Couples\nWent here last night for a few beers, it was nice. \n\nThe place is easy to find, and your welcomed as you exit the lift by a member of staff who helps you select a table, it was really quiet (6pm on a Monday night) so we selected a table outside with the best view. \n\nBeer prices are okay, we paid 140'000 for a jug of Budweiser. This and tiger are the cheapest jugs and the prices increase for other beers. Single beers and towers are also available. \n\nBe aware they do add on 10% though as a tax or service charge? Not too sure, after quite a few jugs I wasn't fussed and was far too merry to argue! Didn't actually realise until I checked my receipt this morning!\n\nTo the person who said it was 'hooters-esque' definately hasn't been to hooters. I've been to many and this couldn't be any less like it. The female waitresses are wearing shorts and t shirts, no cleavage or anything on show. \n\nNice little place, obviously not the same level of view as the skyscraper bars, but good enough if you don't want to part with $8 for a coffee!\nRead more\nWritten April 12, 2016",
